        "lesson": "<p>☐ Body ☐ Breath ☐ Attention ☐ Space</p><p>What I noticed today:</p><p># Appendix — The Rabbit Hole</p><p>The \"Rabbit Hole\" is a collection of optional, deeper texts within the app — contemplative and scientific extensions of the method, for anyone who wants to go further. They are all free. Below, organized by chapter.</p><p>**Body (Ch. 1)**</p><p>- **[The Veils of Being](https://neurodivergent-mindfulness.org/rabbithole/koshas-veils)** — the Matryoshka allegory: five veils, from the physical body to pure consciousness.</p><p>**Breath (Ch. 2)**</p><p>- **[Learning to Ride the Wind](https://neurodivergent-mindfulness.org/rabbithole/riding-the-wind)** — the breath as a wind you accompany, not control.</p><p>- **[The Lute String and the Vagus Nerve](https://neurodivergent-mindfulness.org/rabbithole/polyvagal-middle-way)** — polyvagal theory and the middle way of the nervous system (also relevant to Ch. 7).</p><p>**Attention (Ch. 3)**</p><p>- **[The Soft Gaze: A Door That Does Not Lock](https://neurodivergent-mindfulness.org/rabbithole/soft-gaze-open-hearing)** — how peripheral vision and open hearing regulate the nervous system.</p><p>**Space (Ch. 4)**</p><p>- **[The Wave Is Not the Sea — Until It Lets Go](https://neurodivergent-mindfulness.org/rabbithole/wave-and-sea)** — the distinction between mindfulness (△) and awareness (∞).</p><p>- **[You Are the Path: The Map, the Territory & the Axis](https://neurodivergent-mindfulness.org/rabbithole/you-are-the-path)** — map and territory, and the entry into the now through the axis.</p><p>- **[The Seething Void](https://neurodivergent-mindfulness.org/rabbithole/quantum-void-awareness)** — the quantum void and awareness.</p><p>**The Neurodivergent Mind (Ch. 5)**</p><p>- **[The Truth Behind the Labels: Plato's Cave](https://neurodivergent-mindfulness.org/rabbithole/plato-cave-neurodivergent)** — the allegory of the cave through the lens of neurodivergence.</p><p>- **[The Goose Is Out](https://neurodivergent-mindfulness.org/rabbithole/the-goose-is-out)** — the koan of the goose and masking.</p><p>- **[Never by Force](https://neurodivergent-mindfulness.org/rabbithole/never-force)** — why pressure in practice brings the opposite; the art of the effortless return (the thread of kindness).</p><p>**Stages & Tradition (Ch. 9–10)**</p><p>- **[Dzogchen: The Great Perfection](https://neurodivergent-mindfulness.org/rabbithole/dzogchen-great-perfection)** — an introduction to effortless awareness.</p><p>- **[The Nature of Mind & The Release of Tension](https://neurodivergent-mindfulness.org/rabbithole/dzogchen-nature-of-mind)** — nature of mind, Trekchö, and neuroscience.</p><p>- **[The Forces of the Cosmos, the Axes of the Mind](https://neurodivergent-mindfulness.org/rabbithole/forces-of-the-cosmos)** — the elements/forces and the four axes.</p><p>**About the App Itself**</p><p>- **[What Does Sandbox Mean?](https://neurodivergent-mindfulness.org/rabbithole/what-is-sandbox)** — the framing of the \"safe space for practice.\"</p><p># Epilogue</p><p>This road has no end. It is a way of standing within life, consciously choosing acceptance at every step.</p><p>Every moment can become a small return to gentleness and openness.</p><p>Mindfulness, in the end, is remembering that within you there already exists an open space that holds you as you are.</p><p>This space asks for nothing and rejects nothing — it simply reminds you that you are present, alive, and whole.</p><p>Keep returning. Consistency in small doses is your own greatest act of care.</p>",
